  "text": {
    "paragraphs": [
      "Lily visits Mia in her garden today. Mia has a small garden behind her house. She has two white rabbits in a cage. \"Do you like rabbits?\" asks Lily. \"Yes, I do,\" says Mia. \"They're quiet, and they have long ears.\" Mia feeds them every morning. \"Are they hungry now?\" asks Lily. \"Yes, they are!\" says Mia. She gives them two big carrots.",
      "\"Do you like parrots?\" asks Lily. \"Yes, I do,\" says Mia. \"But parrots are very loud.\" \"I like parrots, too,\" says Lily. \"What about snakes?\" asks Lily. \"Do you like them?\" \"No, I don't!\" says Mia. \"I don't like snakes at all.\" \"I like all animals,\" says Lily. \"Not snakes!\" laughs Mia.",
      "Then a small white kitten comes into the garden. It is Snow, Mia's new kitten. Pip sees the kitten. He likes her, and he wants to play. \"Woof!\" says Pip, and he runs to her. But the kitten doesn't like Pip. She jumps on the cage and looks down. \"Don't be naughty, Pip!\" says Mia. Pip sits down with his nose on the grass. \"Oh, Pip!\" says Lily. Mia smiles. \"A kitten is a good pet,\" she says. \"Pip is a good pet, too.\""
    ],
    "summary": "Mia likes rabbits but she doesn't like snakes. Pip likes Mia's kitten, but the kitten doesn't like Pip.",
